<?xml version='1.0'?>
<!--
  Team-supplied ArUco fiducials on the arena's 80/20 fiducial rail.

  The arena provides only the bare matte-black 1010 rail; the markers and their
  mounts are the team's own kit, attached during setup and removed afterwards
  (guidebook section 4.6.7). Modelled where the guidebook puts the rail:

    rail        X -2.00 .. -0.50 m, on the inside face of the front wall
    height      Z = 0.40 m, "approximately 40 cm (+/- 2.5 cm) above the
                regolith surface" (section 5.7)
    near end    0.50 m west of the Origin Point, which is the centre of the
                front wall and the origin of the arena frame used throughout
                this world

  Marker centres in ARENA coordinates - the table a registration node needs,
  since a detection only helps if you know where the marker is:

    ArUco id    X          Y       Z
    67          -1.7125    0.028   0.40
    68          -1.2500    0.028   0.40
    69          -0.7875    0.028   0.40

  Spacing is a uniform 0.4625 m. That is worth checking against: if two markers
  are visible, their measured separation must match it, which is the cheapest
  guard there is against a false detection teleporting the map frame.

  DICTIONARY: DICT_6X6_100 (OpenCV enum 9), matching
  vision/aruco_detector's DEFAULT_DICTIONARY_ID. 6x6 is chosen over the 4x4
  families on measured margin - minimum inter-marker Hamming distance across
  the whole dictionary, counting all four rotations:

    DICT_4X4_100    3        DICT_5X5_100    7        DICT_6X6_100   12

  The usual reason to prefer 4x4 is detection range, and it does not apply
  here: the starting zone is only 2.25 m deep, so at the far edge a 0.238 m
  marker is 56 px wide on the D455 (640x480, 1.089 rad), which is 7.0 px per
  cell for 6x6 against a ~3-4 px/cell floor. The robustness is free.

  The marker SQUARE is 0.238 m on a 0.35 m plate; the rest is the white quiet
  zone the detector needs to find the contour. Pass 0.238 to
  estimatePoseSingleMarkers, not 0.35 - using the plate size scales every
  recovered translation by 1.47.

  Textures are generated, not the old ARC ones. Those were recovered from git
  first and are undecodable: correct binary patterns, but the black border runs
  to the texture edge with no white quiet zone, so no detector can find them.

  Deliberately no visibility_flags, unlike lunabotics_zones. These are hardware
  the camera has to see; the zone outlines are annotations kept out of
  perception.
-->
<sdf version='1.8'>
  <model name='lunabotics_fiducials'>
    <pose>0 0 0 0 0 0</pose>
    <static>true</static>

    <link name='marker_67'>
      <!-- pitch then yaw turns the plate's face to +Y, i.e. north into the arena -->
      <pose>-1.7125 0.028 0.4 0 1.5708 1.5708</pose>
      <collision name='marker_67_collision'>
        <geometry><box><size>0.35 0.35 0.005</size></box></geometry>
      </collision>
      <visual name='marker_67_visual'>
        <geometry><box><size>0.35 0.35 0.005</size></box></geometry>
        <material>
          <pbr><metal><albedo_map>textures/aruco67.png</albedo_map></metal></pbr>
          <ambient>1 1 1 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>1 1 1 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.05 0.05 0.05 1</specular>
          <emissive>0 0 0 1</emissive>
        </material>
      </visual>
    </link>

    <link name='marker_68'>
      <!-- pitch then yaw turns the plate's face to +Y, i.e. north into the arena -->
      <pose>-1.25 0.028 0.4 0 1.5708 1.5708</pose>
      <collision name='marker_68_collision'>
        <geometry><box><size>0.35 0.35 0.005</size></box></geometry>
      </collision>
      <visual name='marker_68_visual'>
        <geometry><box><size>0.35 0.35 0.005</size></box></geometry>
        <material>
          <pbr><metal><albedo_map>textures/aruco68.png</albedo_map></metal></pbr>
          <ambient>1 1 1 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>1 1 1 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.05 0.05 0.05 1</specular>
          <emissive>0 0 0 1</emissive>
        </material>
      </visual>
    </link>

    <link name='marker_69'>
      <!-- pitch then yaw turns the plate's face to +Y, i.e. north into the arena -->
      <pose>-0.7875 0.028 0.4 0 1.5708 1.5708</pose>
      <collision name='marker_69_collision'>
        <geometry><box><size>0.35 0.35 0.005</size></box></geometry>
      </collision>
      <visual name='marker_69_visual'>
        <geometry><box><size>0.35 0.35 0.005</size></box></geometry>
        <material>
          <pbr><metal><albedo_map>textures/aruco69.png</albedo_map></metal></pbr>
          <ambient>1 1 1 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>1 1 1 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.05 0.05 0.05 1</specular>
          <emissive>0 0 0 1</emissive>
        </material>
      </visual>
    </link>

  </model>
</sdf>
